# DTF tier manifest: curation-global-publisher-trust  (#2948 / #2947 / 1.7.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single. The typed publisher_trust evaluator is
# DB+API-side (curation_rules.config + the evaluate_typed_rules dispatch seam
# consumed by POST /curation/packages/re-evaluate). Storage-independent; no
# external egress required (publisher identity is read from the SEEDED package
# metadata blob, not fetched).
#
# The feature (#2948, integrated by #2947): a GLOBAL publisher_trust rule maps
# a package's publisher against a trusted-publisher allowlist. The publisher is
# extracted from the artifact metadata blob and LABELED with its provenance —
# a registry-verified attestation (strong) vs self-asserted author/maintainer
# metadata (weak, spoofable). Under `match: attestation` (the secure default),
# a self-asserted name on the allowlist is NOT trusted.
#
# CRITICAL — enforcement is at the STAGING-CATALOG / re-evaluate layer, NOT the
# PEP 503 proxy download gate (that gate is pattern-only and skips typed
# rules). So this oracle drives packages through POST /curation/packages/
# re-evaluate and asserts on the resulting CATALOG DECISION / status
# (approved / blocked / review) + rule_id, never a proxy 403 on a pull.
#
# Oracle (discriminating — decision seam, one global rule, four packages):
#   RULE    global publisher_trust {trusted_publishers:["NumFOCUS"],
#           match:"attestation", action:"block"}. 201 + rule_type echoed.
#   ATTEST  pypi pkg with a merged provenance attestation bundle for the
#           NumFOCUS GitHub org -> Allow -> status=approved, rule_id=<rule>.
#   SPOOF   pypi pkg with self-asserted info.author="NumFOCUS" and NO
#           attestation -> Block (spoof-resistant) -> status=blocked,
#           rule_id=<rule>. The dependency-confusion shape a squatter uploads.
#   UNKNOWN pypi pkg on an applicable format with no extractable publisher ->
#           Flag("publisher unknown") -> status=review, rule_id=<rule>.
#   NA      a `raw` (non-applicable) format -> NotApplicable pass-through ->
#           default stance decides it (default_action=allow -> approved) with
#           rule_id NULL: the global rule never judged it.
#
# Discriminating: GREEN on the #2947/#2948 image (the trichotomy
# approved/blocked/review from ONE rule + NULL-rule pass-through). RED on a
# pre-feature baseline: the typed rule is not enforced (config/rule_type
# dropped), so no package is blocked/reviewed by it and the SPOOF stays
# unblocked — a legacy pattern engine cannot render three different statuses
# from a single rule.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: the oracle drives an admin login plus ~15
# back-to-back API/DB calls; the base default (ON) would throttle them.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
